-- title:
--   Regular fibre of the pole chart at ∞-branch cusps, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q=3$, let $M'\neq 0$ be a natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$, and let $\zeta\in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity admitting a ring homomorphism $\iota:L\to\mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\zeta)=\exp(2\pi i/q)$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L((t))$ over $L$ generated by the coefficientwise images under $\mathbb{Q}\to L$ of the $q$-expansion field `xHFunctionField` of level $q^2M'$ and group $H=\ker\bigl((\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times\bigr)$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $q$ lies in $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with uniformiser $\varpi$, $\mathfrak{m}_A=(\varpi)$, and let $K$ carry a compatible $A$-algebra structure. Let $j\in K$ be nonzero with Laurent series the coefficientwise image of `jq`, and let $W_0\subseteq K$ be the valuation subring consisting of those $f$ for which there are power series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ nonzero modulo $\mathfrak{m}_A$ and $f\cdot y=x$ after mapping to $L((t))$. Put $B=$ `chartAlgInf`$(A,K,j)$, the $A$-subalgebra of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$. Then for every prime $y\subseteq B$ containing $\varpi$, containing $j^{-1}$, containing every $b\in B$ whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$, and such that it is NOT the case that for all $b\in B$ whose Laurent series lies in the base change to $L$ of `modularFunctionFieldFull`$(q^2M')$ (the field generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the expansions $j(q^{1/d})$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $q^2M'$) one has $b\in y$ exactly when the constant coefficient of $b$ lies in the image of $\mathfrak{m}_A$: every localisation $B_m$ of $B$ at $y$ is a regular local ring, and so is $B_m$ modulo the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$.
--
--   This is the regularity-with-regular-special-fibre statement for the two-chart integral model of $X_H(q^2M')$ at those cusp centres on the pole ($j^{-1}$) chart whose image on the $X_0(M')$-floor is a cusp other than $\bar\infty$, in the case $q=3$; it is the companion, for the complementary class of primes, of the statement proved for the centres lying over $\bar\infty$. It feeds the verification that the integral model is regular with regular fibre over $\varpi$, which is what the semistability input to the level-lowering argument requires.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_isRegularLocalRing_fibre_of_isLocalization_atPrime_chartAlgInf_of_not_forall_mem_floor_iff_xH_of_isAlgebraic_of_eq_three.lean

